÷3÷The_IDE_Menu_Bar÷The IDE Menu Bar÷Open Watcom Integrated Development Environment
îThe_IDE_Menu_Bar

ìIntegrated Development Environment, menu barì ìmenu bar, Integrated Development Environmentì The IDE's menu bar consists of the following eight menus:

Ê
ÌFile
¹ Open new or existing projects, close and save projects, exit the IDE, and show or hide the toolbar and status bar

ÌActions
¹ Make all targets, run applications, and invoke other GUI Tools

ÌTargets
¹ Work with targets, including setting switches and creating, removing, and renaming targets

ÌSources
¹ Work with sources, including setting switches and creating, removing, and renaming sources

ÌOptions
¹ Set switches for creating targets and sources

ÌLog
¹ Perform functions relating to the IDE Log window

ÌWindow
¹ Refresh the contents of the IDE windows and view the targets currently available on the IDE window

ÌHelp
¹ Access on-line help information
Ë
´
÷3÷The_IDE_Status_Bar÷The IDE Status Bar÷Open Watcom Integrated Development Environment
îThe_IDE_Status_Bar

ìIntegrated Development Environment, status barì ìstatus bar, Integrated Development Environmentì The Status Bar appears along the bottom of the Open Watcom IDE Project window.  This bar displays hint text for the toolbar button and menu option over which your cursor is positioned.  Status messages, such as Saving, Adding, and Executing Log, appear in this bar so you are aware of what action the IDE is performing.  A check mark beside the Show Status Bar menu option in the File menu indicates that this feature is enabled.  To disable this feature, choose the option again from the File menu and the status bar disappears from the window.

courier12°c°ide2.bmp°helv10
ïibïFigure 2.ğïibïğïbï The IDE Status Bar can be toggled from the File menu.ğ
´
÷3÷The_IDE_Toolbar÷The IDE Toolbar÷Open Watcom Integrated Development Environment
îThe_IDE_Toolbar

ìIntegrated Development Environment, tool barì ìtool bar, Integrated Development Environmentì In the Open Watcom IDE Project window, the toolbar appears below the menu bar when the Show Tool Bar option in the File menu is activated (default).  A check mark beside the menu option indicates that it is enabled.  To disable this feature, choose the option again from the File menu and the toolbar disappears.

courier12°c°ide3.bmp°helv10
ïibïFigure 3.ğïibïğïbï You can access thirteen IDE functions from the toolbar.ğ

The following explains the function each icon performs, as well as the equivalent function on the menu bar.

Ê
ÌCreate
¹ °i°newproj.bmp° ìnew projectì Create a new project.  This is equivalent to the option New Project in the File menu.

ÌOpen
¹ °i°openproj.bmp° ìopen projectì Open an existing project.  This is equivalent to the option Open Project in the File menu.

ÌSave
¹ °i°saveproj.bmp° ìsave projectì Save the current project.  This is equivalent to the option Save Project in the File menu.

ÌEdit
¹ °i°edititem.bmp° ìedit textì Edit the selected source file.  This is equivalent to the option Edit Text in the Sources menu.

ÌMake Source
¹ °i°makeitem.bmp° ìmake sourceì Make the selected source file.  This is equivalent to the option Make in the Sources menu.

ÌMake Target
¹ °i°maketarg.bmp° ìmake targetì Make the current target.  This is equivalent to the option Make in the Targets menu.

ÌRun
¹ °i°runtarg.bmp° ìrun targetì Run the current target.  This is equivalent to the option Run in the Targets menu.

ÌDebug
¹ °i°debgtarg.bmp° ìdebug targetì Debug the current target.  This is equivalent to the option Debug in the Targets menu.

ÌRemote Debug
¹ °i°rdbgtarg.bmp° ìremote debug targetì Debug the current target on a remote machine.  This is equivalent to the option Remote Debug in the Targets menu.

ÌBrowse
¹ °i°browtarg.bmp° ìbrowse targetì Browse the current target.  This is equivalent to the option Browse in the Targets menu.  Currently, browsing is supported by the Open Watcom C/C++ compilers only (Open Watcom FORTRAN 77 does not support browsing).

ÌSample
¹ °i°samptarg.bmp° ìsample targetì Run and sample the current target.  This is equivalent to the option Sample in the Targets menu.

ÌProfile
¹ °i°proftarg.bmp° ìprofile targetì Profile the current target.  This is equivalent to the option Profile in the Targets menu.

ÌMake All
¹ °i°makeproj.bmp° ìmake all targetsì Make all targets in the project.  This is equivalent to the option Make All in the Actions menu.
