îReview_of_What_Happened

ìIntegrated Development Environment, tutorial reviewì In this session, you created a project calledcourier12 first.wpj.helv10  This project had one target calledcourier12 target1.exe,helv10 a 32-bit Windows executable (unless you specified another target type).  Using the Open Watcom Editor, you entered and edited the source text in a file calledcourier12 source1.chelv10 orcourier12 source1.forhelv10 (if you tried the FORTRAN example).  You compiled and linked it into an executable program using the Open Watcom Make utility, a Open Watcom compiler, and the Open Watcom Linker.  You ran it directly and under the control of the Open Watcom Debugger.

When you saved the project, the Open Watcom Integrated Development Environment created the following permanent files:

