÷2÷The_Open_Watcom_IDE_Project_Window÷The Open Watcom IDE Project Window÷Open Watcom Integrated Development Environment
îThe_Open_Watcom_IDE_Project_Window

ìIntegrated Development Environment, project windowì ìproject window, Integrated Development Environmentì When you first start the Open Watcom Integrated Development Environment, an empty Open Watcom IDE Project window opens.  This window represents the project that is currently open in the IDE.  The name of the current project appears in the title bar of this window.

The first thing you need to do is open a project for the Open Watcom IDE Project window.  This can be a new project you create or an existing project you open.

Ê
ÌImportant:
¹ You can have only one project open at a time in the IDE.  If you attempt to open or create a project while one already exists in the IDE window, a message box appears informing you that the IDE is closing the current project and asks if you want to save any changes made to that project.  Choose Yes, No, or Cancel in this box to continue.
Ë
´
÷3÷Opening_a_Project÷Opening a Project÷Open Watcom Integrated Development Environment
îOpening_a_Project

ìIntegrated Development Environment, opening a projectì ìopening a projectì

Ê
ÌTo create a new project:
¹  ìnew projectì

Ì(1)
¹ïbï Choose New Projectğ from the File menu.

The Enter Project Filename dialog appears on the screen where you enter the name of the project you are creating.

Ì(2)
¹ïbï Enter the desired nameğ in the File Name field and choose the desired directory.

All projects must have the extension ".wpj".

courier12°c°ide11.bmp°helv10
ïibïFigure 11.ğïibïğïbï Use the Enter Project Filename dialog to create a new project.ğ

Ì(3)
¹ïbï Click on OKğ when completed.

The Enter Project Filename dialog closes and the new project name appears in the title bar of the Open Watcom IDE Project window.  A New Target dialog opens on the screen where you add a target to the new project.  Refer to the section Adding a Target for more information.
Ë

Ê
ÌTo open an existing project:
¹  ìopen projectì

Ì(1)
¹ïbï Choose Open Projectğ from the File menu.

The Open dialog appears on the screen where you select the project you want to open.

courier12°c°ide12.bmp°helv10
ïibïFigure 12.ğïibïğïbï Use the Open dialog to open an existing project.ğ

Ì(2)
¹ïbï Choose the desired project.ğ

All projects have the extension ".wpj".

Ì(3)
¹ïbï Click on OKğ when the desired project appears in the File Name field.

The Open dialog closes and the name of the selected project appears in the title bar of the Open Watcom IDE Project window.  If targets exist for the selected project, windows representing the targets appear in the main window.
Ë
